# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in. Never commit the real file.

# Free key from https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
# 32 lowercase hex characters.
# Without it the FRED client falls back to the keyless fredgraph.csv
# endpoint, which is fine for daily pulls but slower and less reliable for
# the multi-year historical backfill at M8.
FRED_API_KEY=

# SEC requires a descriptive User-Agent with a contact address on every
# request (N-PORT bulk downloads, XBRL, EDGAR full-text search).
SEC_USER_AGENT=Your Name your@email.com

# Where the stock-analysis-model run snapshots (results_*.json) live. Read
# point-in-time by data/issuer_fundamentals.py so a bond's fundamentals match
# the date its ~98-day-old N-PORT mark was struck.
#
# This repo is standalone, so the equity checkout can be anywhere. The code
# falls back to ~/Desktop/Workspace Folder/output, which is right on this
# machine and wrong everywhere else -- set it here rather than relying on that.
# If it points nowhere the divergence signal is silently suppressed for every
# bond rather than erroring, so if divergence has gone flat across the whole
# universe, check this first.
EQUITY_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/path/to/stock-analysis-model/output
